4n3tp6t7q.12896">Two design choices worth saying out loud to judges. First,=
 one <code spellcheck=3D"false" autocorrect=3D"off" autocapitalize=3D"off">=
expiresAt</code> copied onto every document means TTL deletes the whole roo=
m with no cascade code; ending early is one <code spellcheck=3D"false" auto=
correct=3D"off" autocapitalize=3D"off">updateMany</code> per collection. Se=
cond, when a file is uploaded its extracted text goes into a <code spellche=
ck=3D"false" autocorrect=3D"off" autocapitalize=3D"off">messages</code> doc=
ument of kind <code spellcheck=3D"false" autocorrect=3D"off" autocapitalize=
=3D"off">file</code>, so a single vector index covers chat and files and th=
e Free cluster's 3-index budget holds.</p><p data-bid=3D"ms4n3tp6t7q.13285"=
><strong>Joining by PIN without accounts</strong></p><ol data-bid=3D"ms4n3t=
p6t7q.13317"><li><div><p data-bid=3D"ms4n3tp6t7q.13319">Host creates a room=
. The server draws the PIN with <code spellcheck=3D"false" autocorrect=3D"o=
ff" autocapitalize=3D"off">crypto.randomInt(0, 1000000)</code> and retries =
on a duplicate-key error, makes a 128-bit <code spellcheck=3D"false" autoco=
rrect=3D"off" autocapitalize=3D"off">joinSecret</code> for the QR link, and=
 a 256-bit host token. Only SHA-256 hashes of tokens are stored.</p></div><=
/li><li><div><p data-bid=3D"ms4n3tp6t7q.13550">The QR encodes <code spellch=
eck=3D"false" autocorrect=3D"off" autocapitalize=3D"off">/j/&lt;joinSecret&=
gt;</code>, which cannot be guessed. The 6-digit PIN is the fallback for ty=
ping.</p></div></li><li><div><p data-bid=3D"ms4n3tp6t7q.13652"><code spellc=
heck=3D"false" autocorrect=3D"off" autocapitalize=3D"off">POST /join</code>=
 with PIN and nickname is rate-limited to 5 attempts per minute per IP and =
only works while the room is <code spellcheck=3D"false" autocorrect=3D"off"=
 autocapitalize=3D"off">open</code>.</p></div></li><li><div><p data-bid=3D"=
